  "articleBody": "Upgrading garage walls, lighting, and floors can sometimes look manageable on the surface, but certain warning signs indicate you need professional general contracting expertise rather than quick cosmetic patches. Recognizing these issues early saves money and ensures the finished garage remains safe and code-compliant.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps:\n- Visible moisture or water intrusion: If water seeps under the sill plates or through foundation cracks, the building envelope must be sealed before hanging insulation.\n- Electrical panel upgrades: Adding 240V circuits for welders, heavy compressors, or heating units demands proper subpanel planning and qualified trade execution.\n- Framing alterations and ceiling storage: Hanging substantial overhead storage or cutting into roof trusses requires structural verification so roof loads are never compromised.\n- Damaged drywall and fire separation: The wall separating your garage from the home must maintain a strict fire-rated drywall assembly without gaps or penetrations.\n\nAbraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC brings hands-on framing, drywall installation, painting, and trim expertise to every job, coordinating trade partners seamlessly. Call 303-505-0866 today to schedule an on-site consultation for your garage upgrade in the Denver area.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}